From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hisamiii <265242552+hisamiii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] loom: add a fill's second egress lane

A second constrain.fill of a streamed interleaved panel: the second source rides on its worker's merged C egress channel (the same core memory-to-stream channel and route, its own ring and descriptors), and the panel gets a second memory-tile writer on the stream-to-memory channel where that C egress lands: the odd interleave units in one strided descriptor, queued per push before the C ring (both rings then run per push), freeing a done lock that the first writer (now the even units) waits on before it releases the panel; it starts on a go lock that the first writer's first unit releases past the panel's credit. LOOM_EXP_DMA_DUMP=1 (diag): the DMA, staged channel and column 0 lock plans.
---

